WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
Who was the director?

2
00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:02.840
John A. Cox.

3
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.960
I replaced John A. Cox.

4
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.280
I didn’t replace him, I became director after he retired.

5
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.860
And I remember telling him, I said, “Johnny, do you see all these people here?”

6
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.280
I said, “Every little kid in there has two parents with him.

7
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.360
And probably a grandmother and a granddad with them.

8
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.540
And we don’t have any place for them.”

9
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:37.920
And I said the people then in the coliseum, in the livestock show, you had just one kid, an animal,

10
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:48.800
an agent, and the specialist . . . we showed more attention to that aspect of the show because it was glamorous.

11
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:58.260
And these kids back there, they were just as worthy of our attention as the one who was going to show the grand champion steer.

12
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.680
He could show that little lamb over there which was, you know, very inexpensive,

13
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.860
but it got the kid involved just as much or better than the other.

14
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.000
And I made that note to him, and he says, “You know, you’re right.”

15
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:25.040
And he went to work through the legislature and other things and within a few years we had the Sheep and Swine building built.

16
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.780
I don’t want to take credit for it, that’s not my point.

17
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.220
But it’s a point we need to make.

18
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:42.580
We had to acknowledge the fact that these young kids with the very inexpensive project were just as important as the kid who was going to show the grand champion animal.
